# stackwrangler AI workflow

Public in-repo defaults for agents. Private maintainer board claiming is **not** required for external contributors.

## Branch

```bash
git checkout main && git pull origin main
git checkout -b feature/<issue>-<short-slug>
```

## Versioning (pillars + release label + scores)

- **Milestone** = pillar (`Platform`, `Identity & authz`, …) — `docs/version-plan.md`.
- **Label** = product cut (`v0.0.2` Public, `v0.0.3` Trust, `v0.0.4` Accuracy, `v0.0.5` Security/deps, `v0.0.6` Maturity/testing, `v0.1.0` Org path) only if theme + Impact gate match; else **no version label**.
- New / Debt: pillar + `./bin/issue-score.sh`; **do not** auto-add `$(cat docs/CURRENT_RELEASE)`.
- Absorb small gaps in-parent (`docs/gap-check.md`); Debt is evaluate-and-place.
- Cut a release: `./bin/release-tag.sh vX.Y.Z --next vA.B.C` — only when asked; then `./bin/check-current-release.sh`. Details: `docs/versioning.md`.

## Product north star

`docs/vision.md` — long-term feel (not a ticket).
OpenSpec changes are for **one delivery**; don’t park the whole product vision there.

CLI entry is `./bin/stackwrangler` (`./bin/awsbox` is a one-line shim). Prefer `STACKWRANGLER_*` env vars; some `AWSBOX_*` names remain as fallbacks.

## OpenSpec

- On `main`: `/opsx-propose` → `openspec/changes/<change-name>/`
- Delivery branch: `/opsx-apply` against `tasks.md`
- Grow `openspec/specs/` as shipped behaviour (archive changes separately)

## Open Design (required before web UI)

Any ticket that adds or changes **console / web UI** (`console/`, new service pages, chrome) must go through Open Design **before** React implementation:

1. Theme: `design/stackwrangler/` (grey rose). Do not invent a new palette or copy AWS orange / sky blue / smile.
2. Mocks: `./bin/od-design-run.sh --issue <n> "…"`. Prefer skill **web-clone** when the screen exists in real AWS. Read-only AWS console screenshots are allowed; never create/update/delete real resources without explicit approval.
3. **Dead controls:** a button/link that is not wired yet must be `disabled` with `title="To implement"` (and a Debt ticket if it belongs in v1). If we will never ship it, omit from the mock — do not leave an enabled control that does nothing or only toasts.
4. Land HTML under `design/stackwrangler-console/` (or the ticket’s design folder).
5. Then implement against the mocks.

Never raw `curl` for OD runs — always `./bin/od-design-run.sh`.

## Commits / PRs

- No `Co-authored-by` / Cursor attribution
- PR body: `Closes #<n>`
- After merge or abandon: delete remote + local head branch, remove worktree, `git fetch --prune`. Prefer `gh pr merge … --delete-branch`. No leftover merged `feature/*` / `batch/*` on origin. Orchestrator: `./bin/batch-cleanup.sh all --force`. Never `git clean -fdx` (wipes `.git/info/exclude`); private notes → local exclude only, not public `.gitignore`.

## Gap check before merge (required)

User relies on the agent to not lose half-baked follow-ups (especially UI stubs).

**Before** merge / treating the ticket as finished:

```bash
./bin/gap-check.sh <n>
```

1. Walk the checklist in `docs/gap-check.md`
2. Prefer absorbing small additive gaps into this PR. Otherwise `Debt: … (from #<n>)` with pillar + Impact/Effort; release label only if cut gate matches. Tracker + docs link. Console debt: Open Design `web-clone` (`./bin/od-design-run.sh`)
3. Prefer shipping docs in the PR; if blocked on public docs / screenshot / interaction edge → `Doc: … (from #<n>)` per `docs/docs-catalog.md` (skill `docs-catalog`; Agent `cursor-batch-docs`). User-facing host/ports/Docker copy is **Linux-first** (not WSL-led; #491).
4. Mention new Debt / Doc issues (or absorbed) in the PR body

Do **not** treat the parent as finished until gaps are absorbed, ticketed, or explicitly N/A in the PR.

## Maintainers

`bin/board-status.sh` / `bin/issue-score.sh` may remain in-repo for maintainers who have private GitHub project access. Board claiming / Agent field / project URLs are **not** part of this public rule. Lifecycle: **Backlog** → **Designing** → **In progress** → **In review** → **Done** (`ready` aliases to backlog; do not rewrite Status option IDs).
